  itemIcon: {fileID: -7814240041180328124, guid: 24e104b99eebd544493c6326faca2c58, type: 3}
  description: 'The Divine Currency of Ancient Greece

    According to legend, the
    forebears of Zeus hurled a bolt of divine lightning into a gold mine on the slopes
    of Mount Olympus. This celestial impact imbued the ore with a unique, radiant
    stigma. Mortals later adopted this glowing gold as a sacred currency, utilizing
    its unearthly luminescence as a natural and infallible seal of authenticity.'
